"How long the wire rests between one full pass — sweep, browse, knock — and the next. Shorter keeps the pressure continuous; longer revisits on a slower, quieter cadence. While the wire stays quiet the rest stretches itself, up to ten minutes, and snaps back the moment a pass finds something." = "Le temps que le fil se repose entre un passage complet — balayage, navigation, frappe — et le suivant. Plus court garde la dérive petite et coûte plus de batterie et tes propres émissions permanentes.";
